bar 120 high)", "always_in": "long", "notes": "H4 context (current, decision_time_ms 1789991999999) and D1 context (current, decision_time_ms 1789948799999) both read bull-trend/breakout-spike; D1 context is used only for the 2771 spike-high location, and raw closed M15/H1 bars are the entry evidence."}, "setup": {"type": "breakout pullback: buy the breakout of the 21-bar M15 tight range that has held above the broken 2700 H4 double top", "trigger_status": "pending", "signal_quality": "weak", "location_assessment": "neutral", "no_trade_reason": null}, "decision_timeframe": "M15", "context_timeframes_used": ["H1", "M15", "H4", "D1"], "entry_mechanism": "breakout_pullback", "trigger": {"reference": "M15 bar 119 high (range high)", "price_field": "high", "price": "2747.76", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 119, "open_time_ms": 1790001900000, "close_time_ms": 1790002799999}, "kind": "stop", "direction": "above"}, "invalidation": {"reference": "M15 bar 117 low (low of the recent higher-low cluster 2718.09/2720.15/2718.23; back into the middle of the tight range)", "price_field": "low", "price": "2718.09", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 117, "open_time_ms": 1790000100000, "close_time_ms": 1790000999999}}, "evidence_for": ["M15 bar 119 (open 2733.06, close 2734.92) is the highest close of the 21-bar consolidation and takes out the prior range highs: 2739.54 (bar 112), 2741.55 (bar 115), 2742.56 (bar 118), then 2747.76 (bar 119) - range highs are rising into the close.", "The M15 range since the spike bar 98 (open 2708.33, high 2850, low 2702.56, close 2739.13) has held entirely above 2702.56, i.e. above the H4 2700 zone that had been tagged twice (H4 bar 108 high 2700, H4 bar 118 high 2700) - a tight consolidation above a broken double top, not a pullback below it.", "H1 follow-through per the H4 transition condition: H1 bars 117-119 (open_time 1789992000000 / 1789995600000 / 1789999200000) closed 2734.09, 2734.13, 2734.92, all above the H4 breakout bar's close 2723.15, with lows 2719.08 / 2720.15 / 2718.09 above 2700.", "H1 bar 119 (open 2734.63, high 2747.76, low 2718.09, close 2734.92) makes a higher high versus H1 bar 118 high 2741.55 and closes at the top of the last five H1 bars (lows 2709.56, 2713.04, 2719.08, 2720.15, 2718.09 all hold above 2700).", "M15 lows have stopped falling under the range: 2718.23 (bar 116), 2718.09 (bar 117), 2731.83 (bar 118), 2731.83 (bar 119), so a stop below 2718.09 is a defensible structural invalidation with a defined 29.67-point risk from the 2747.76 trigger."], "evidence_against": ["M15 bar 98 printed 2850 and closed 2739.13, a 147.44-point bar with a 110.87-point upper tail; the whole 21-bar range sits inside that tail, so the buy trigger 2747.76 is still 102.24 below a level that was just rejected.", "H4 bar 120 (open 2658.81, high 2850, low 2658.06, close 2723.15) left a 126.85-point upper tail with no follow-through bar in the window; the H4 context flags two earlier upside spikes (bar 61 high 2680, bar 81 high 2609.02) that were fully retraced.", "Overhead structure crowds the setup versus its invalidation: 2747.76 is only 5.20 above the prior M15 range high 2742.56 and only 23.24 below the 2771 D1 spike high, against a 29.67-point stop distance.", "Bar 119 is a weak breakout bar, not a bull trend bar closing on its high: its close 2734.92 sits in the lower ~19% of its 2731.83-2747.76 range with a 12.84 upper tail.", "The 21-bar M15 range is only about 45 points (1.6%) and oscillates around the H4 breakout bar's close 2723.15 - consistent with balance at the breakout level, and tight-range breakouts frequently fail without a strong breakout bar."], "qualitative_confidence": "medium", "uncertainty": ["Whether the M15 tight range resolves upward or becomes a final flag: no bar in the supplied packet closes above 2747.76, so the breakout is untriggered and unconfirmed.", "The would-be signal bar is already printed (bar 119) and is marginal (new high by 5.20 with a 12.84 upper tail); a stronger bull bar closing on its high would raise confidence in the same trigger.", "The D1 context is 15 hours older than the frozen decision time and its 2771/2557 levels are contextual descriptions; the D1 spike high 2771 was exceeded only by a wick (M15 bar 98 high 2850) with no close above it."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["A M15 close back below 2731.83 (bar 119 low) and then below 2718.09 (bar 117 low) would mark a failed breakout of the range high and void the long case.", "A M15/H1 close below 2702.56 (bar 98 low) would break the three-hour acceptance above the H4 2700 zone and return price to the prior H4 wide range.", "Repeated M15 closes between 2718.09 and 2747.76 without exceeding 2747.76 would keep the tight-range read and argue against a breakout.", "A M15 close above 2747.76 with the low holding above 2731.83 would confirm the breakout and shift the focus to 2771 and then 2850."]}, "latest_trader_intent": {"schema": "brooks.trade-intent.v2", "role": "TRADER", "decision": "NO_TRADE", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1790009999999, "market_context": {"regime": "bull-trend", "phase": "post-climax consolidation", "h1": "bull flag / tight range holding above 2709", "h4": "bull-trend breakout-spike, bar 118 spiked to 2850", "d1": "bull-trend breakout-spike above 2557.46", "location": "mid-range below two faded spike highs"}, "setup": {"type": "trading_range_midrange_after_climax", "trigger_status": "absent", "signal_quality": "weak", "location_assessment": "poor", "no_trade_reason": "poor_location"}, "decision_timeframe": null, "context_timeframes_used": ["M15", "H1", "H4", "D1"], "entry_mechanism": "none", "trigger": null, "invalidation": null, "evidence_for": ["M15 bar 90 (open 2708.33, high 2850, close 2739.13) spiked and closed 110.87 below its high; M15 bar 115 (open 2744.20, high 2795, close 2754.31) repeated it closing 40.69 below its high - two failed upside pushes leaving long upper tails.", "M15 bar 115 high 2795 is a lower high versus M15 bar 90 high 2850, so post-climax structure is two-sided rather than a clean continuation.", "The last ten M15 bars overlap tightly between ~2709 and ~2765 with no decisive close at the range top; current M15 bar 119 (open 2757.71, high 2763.34, low 2751.00, close 2753.69) is a bear bar closing near its low.", "Price 2753.69 sits mid-range between the ~2702.56/2709.56 lows and the 2850 high - the middle of a range, not an edge, so a with-trend entry here is poorly located."], "evidence_against": ["D1 and H4 contexts are both bull-trend/breakout-spike with Always-In long and rising swing lows (2358.62 -> 2495.82 -> 2568.16 -> 2658.06); H1 bars 106-119 hold above the 2643-2720 breakout with higher lows at 2713/2718/2730/2742.", "H1 closes rise into the decision bar (2723.15, 2734.09, 2734.13, 2734.92, 2754.31), so a with-trend pending buy-stop above M15 bar 117 high 2765.34 with invalidation below the 2742.00 low would be a conventional bull-flag continuation trigger; the trend lean alone is not disqualifying."], "qualitative_confidence": "medium", "uncertainty": ["Whether the faded 2850/2795 spikes mark a tradable bull flag or the start of a higher trading range is not resolved by the supplied closed bars.", "The immediate M15 bar 119 is a bear bar, so no untriggered buy setup has yet confirmed at this location."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["An M15 close above 2765.34, especially above 2795, would turn the tight range into a continuation and support a breakout entry.", "An M15 close below 2742.00 and then 2709.56 would confirm the faded-spike read and shift toward a pullback/trading range.", "Continued tight overlap between 2742.00 and 2765.34 keeps the middle-of-range read and favors standing aside."]}, "latest_market_context": {"schema": "brooks.market-context.v1", "role": "HTF_ANALYST", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1789948799999, "timeframe": "D1", "observations": ["Window opens at 2116.86 and falls to 1368.42 (bar 13 low, close 1568.55), then reverses; final close 2642.90 is about +24.9% versus the first open and about +93% above the window low.", "Bars 87-89 are the spike: 1916.51 to 2252.16, 2252.20 to 2326.32, 2326.31 to 2515.30, with the window high 2771 printed on bar 89.", "Bars 90-116 are two-sided: overlapping bodies, highs at 2557.46 (bar 95) and 2609.02 (bar 113), lows clustered 2357.18-2425.44; bar 110 spiked to 2680 and closed 2514.72 back inside the range.", "Bars 117-119 close 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 \u2014 the first consecutive closes above the 2557.46 ceiling; bar 117 has open 2446.22, high 2643.52, low 2436.87, range 206.65, closing in its top quarter; bar 118 reaches 2700.", "Bar 119 (open 2632.98, high 2645.88, low 2568.16, close 2642.90) is a 77.72-range bar closing near its high while holding above the range ceiling; it makes a lower high than bar 118 (2645.88 vs 2700).", "Recent lows rise: 2357.18 (bar 101), 2358.62 (bar 114), 2370.54 (bar 115), 2413.82 (bar 116), 2436.87 (bar 117), 2568.16 (bar 119).", "Price 2642.90 remains below the bar-89 spike high 2771, so the post-spike section is not yet a confirmed new-high trend."], "evidence_against": ["The breakout is only three bars; the preceding 27 bars overlap heavily and the region 2357-2557 can still be read as the operating trading range rather than broken.", "Two earlier upside probes failed to hold: bar 110 high 2680 closed 2514.72, bar 113 high 2609.02 closed 2514.07, so upside spikes in this region have recently been rejected.", "2642.90 remains below the bar-89 spike high 2771, so the whole post-spike section can be read as one broad trading range whose upper extreme has not been exceeded.", "Bar 119 makes a lower high than bar 118 (2645.88 vs 2700) with a lower tail to 2568.16, a pause rather than a strong continuation bar, and bar 114 had just traded down to 2358.62 four bars before the breakout."], "uncertainty": ["V2 D1 context adapted for the V1 PM input."]}, "management_history": [{"schema": "brooks.management-decision.v2", "role": "POSITION_MANAGER", "decision_time_ms": 1790005679999, "action": "HOLD", "position_ids": ["wf-main-5"], "reason": "The snapshot is coherent: one MAIN LONG leg (wf-main-5, 0.159) matches the executor's position_id, hedge_state is single_main with no unresolved legs, margin_health is SAFE, and management_policy sets strategy_stop_required false, so the absence of an open stop order is policy-compliant. The recorded premise (breakout above the M15 range high 2747.76 with structural invalidation at 2718.09) is not contradicted: the most recent closed M15 bars hold above 2718.09 and the 1790004600000 bar (close 2744.21) closes near its high after the 2730.50 pullback low. No unmet management condition requires an allowed intervention, so HOLD is the safest coherent step.", "evidence": {"observations": ["Single MAIN position wf-main-5, ETH-USDT LONG 0.159, entry 2749.714944, mark 2749.44, unrealized PnL -0.043716096; ownership_role MAIN and as_of_ms 1790005679999 equal decision_time_ms.", "hedge_state: structure_status single_main, unresolved false, main_side LONG, hedge_side null, hedge_ratio 0, net_exposure 437.16096 USD, gross_exposure_usd 437.16096, ratio_basis absolute_mark_notional.", "executor wf-exec-9 is RUNNING for position wf-main-5 with config stop_price 2718.090000 and target_price 2812.140000, matching the recorded invalidation low 2718.09 (M15 bar 117 low); open_orders is empty and recent_fills shows one FILLED 0.159 buy at 2749.714944 (fee 0.17488) for wf-main-5.", "management_policy brooks-pm-v1:brooks-walkforward-10d, strategy_stop_required false, allowed_management_actions include HOLD; margin_health SAFE with equity 9991.20 and available_margin 9903.77; latest_market_context D1 still reads bull-trend/breakout-spike with price below the 2771 spike high; market_analysis is null.", "Latest closed M15 bars: 1790002800000 close 2747.33 (bull bar at the range high), 1790003700000 close 2731.84 (bar rejecting 2747.33 down to low 2730.50), 1790004600000 close 2744.21 (bull bar closing near its high, low 2730.01); price remains above the 2718.09 invalidation and below the 2771 overhead level."], "evidence_for": ["The documented premise is intact on the supplied closed bars: since the 2747.76 range-high takeout, price has not closed below the 2718.09 invalidation, and the newest closed bar (1790004600000, close 2744.21) recovers to the top of its range after the 2730.50 pullback low.", "Account and policy facts support no intervention: margin_health SAFE, available_margin 9903.77 versus 437.16 USD gross exposure, structure_status single_main with unresolved false, and strategy_stop_required false so the empty open_orders list is not an unmet risk condition.", "State is internally consistent: live quantity 0.159 equals the executor's position_id wf-main-5 mapping and equals the single FILLED fill quantity, with no partial fill or contradictory order/fill record."], "evidence_against": ["No protective order appears in open_orders, so the 2718.09 stop exists only as executor config; if it is not live at the venue, a fast drop through 2718.09 would be unmitigated, which argues for caution or reconciliation rather than complacency.", "The breakout has yet to show strong follow-through: price is slightly below entry 2749.71, the 1790003700000 bar was a rejection bar down to 2730.50, and price is still below the D1 2771 level, so a final-flag/failed-breakout resolution remains a live possibility and would argue for reducing rather than holding."]}, "risk": {"exposure_before": ["ETH-USDT LONG 0.159 at mark 2749.44, ~437.16 USD mark notional, unhedged (hedge_ratio 0)"], "exposure_after": ["ETH-USDT LONG 0.159 at mark 2749.44, ~437.16 USD mark notional, unhedged (hedge_ratio 0)"], "protection_status": "adequate", "costs_considered": ["Taker fill fee already incurred on wf-fill-9 (0.17488 USDT); further fees apply to any reduce/close/hedge leg.", "Funding carry applies to the 0.15